---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms — Ship Studio"
  description="Terms of use for Ship Studio software and this website."
  path="/legal/terms"
>
  <section class="section legal">
    <h1>Terms</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Ship Studio is MIT-licensed open source. This site documents the tool. There is no public
      paid checkout until the operator enables Paddle env and publishes a sale policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      The software is provided under the <a href="https://github.com/Dendro-X0/ship-studio/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT License</a>
      in the repository. You may clone, build, and run it without a Solo purchase. Packaged GitHub
      Releases are the supported download path.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are responsible for vendor accounts (Cloudflare, Vercel, Polar, Paddle, Apple, and others),
      secrets, and those vendors’ terms. Ship Studio does not create API keys, does not store secret
      values in <code>.ship/</code>, and does not replace vendor dashboards.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a Paddle checkout is configured later, that purchase is a contract with Paddle for that
      transaction; license-file issuance is described in the repo’s license-refund dogfood notes.
      Until then, these terms do not sell a Solo SKU.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
